WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.906
[dramatic synthetic music]

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:12.212
[deep tones]

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:24.424
[narrator]
Up until about 20 years ago

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.893
tiny computers,
smart phones, instant

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:29.229
messaging and video conferencing

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:32.365
were all fanciful science
fiction inventions.

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:34.834
Now they're so ubiquitous we

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:37.037
hardly give them
a second thought.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.607
Most of these technologies are
good for mankind

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:45.278
but as with everything it
can be misused and turned

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:49.849
into nefarious tech that
can haunt us our entire lives.

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.552
[dramatic synthesized music]

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:04.898
[ominous music]

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:14.707
[disconcerting music]

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:28.288
In the past 50 years, technology
has leaped forward from the

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:32.792
transistor radio to cell phones
and satellite communication.

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:36.696
Weapons have advanced as well as
surveillance systems.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:40.166
Today anyone can have
their 15 minutes of fame

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.070
just by streaming a video
of themselves worldwide.

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:48.575
We get our news instantly,
we can talk globally to anyone

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:52.512
and we have medical inventions
to make our lives better.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:56.883
But in the hands of
scrupulous people these same

00:01:56.916 --> 00:02:00.320
technologies can be used
to track our every move,

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.823
motivate us to vote in a
specific direction,

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:07.093
invade our bodies and spy on us.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.669
We have become dependent on the

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:18.972
technologies we
take for granted

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:21.107
and those
technologies are poised

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:23.243
to take over the
world we live in

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.812
and perhaps make us their
minions.

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.213
[ominous music]

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:31.017
One of the most relevant
theories is that artificial

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:34.120
intelligence may one
day take over the world.

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:36.789
An AI takeover
is a hypothetical

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:38.925
scenario in which artificial

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.127
intelligence
becomes the dominant

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:43.296
form of intelligence on Earth.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:46.599
With computers or
robots effectively taking the

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:50.236
control of the planet away
from the human species.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.673
Possible scenarios
include replacement

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.109
of the entire human work force,

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:58.978
takeover by a super intelligent
AI

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:02.215
and the popular notion of a
robot uprising.

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:05.952
Some public figures
such as Stephen Hawking

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:09.155
and Elon Musk have
advocated research into

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:12.692
precautionary measures
to ensure future super

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:16.596
intelligent machines
remain under human control.

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:18.364
[ominous music]

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:22.435
The AI control problem
is the issue of how to

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:26.105
build a super intelligent
agent that will aid it's

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:29.242
creators and avoid
inadvertently building a

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:32.779
super intelligence that
will harm its creators.

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.882
Some scholars
argue that solutions

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:38.084
to the control problem might

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:40.553
also find applications
in existing

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:42.589
non-super intelligent AI.

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:48.194
Major approaches to the control
problem include alignment,

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:52.565
which aims to align AI goal
systems with human values

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:56.569
and capability control
which aims to reduce an AI's

00:03:56.603 --> 00:04:00.406
systems capacity to harm
humans or gain control.

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:06.045
An example of capability control
is to research whether a super

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:07.947
intelligent AI could be

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:10.883
successfully
combined in an AI box.

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:13.319
According to Bostrom, such

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:15.755
capability control
proposals are not

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:18.258
reliable or
sufficient to solve the

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:20.693
control problem
in the long term

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.796
but may potentially
act as valuable

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:26.499
supplements to
alignment efforts.

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:32.205
Physicist Stephen Hawking,
Microsoft founder Bill

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:35.875
Gates and Space X founder
Elon Musk have expressed

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:39.712
concerns about the possibility
that AI could develop

00:04:39.746 --> 00:04:43.216
to the point that humans
could not control it.

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:46.052
With Hawking
theorizing that this

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:48.855
could spell the end
of the human race.

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:51.658
[disconcerting music]

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:57.297
Stephen Hawking said in
2014 that success in creating

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:01.134
AI would be the biggest
event in human history.

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:05.204
Unfortunately it
might also be the last

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:08.174
unless we learn
how to avoid the risks.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:14.080
Hawking believed that
in the coming decades,

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:17.483
AI could offer incalculable
benefits and risks.

00:05:17.784 --> 00:05:20.787
Such as technology
outsmarting financial

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.756
markets,
out inventing human researchers,

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:27.160
out manipulating human
leaders and developing

00:05:27.193 --> 00:05:30.229
weapons that we
cannot even understand.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:36.636
In January 2015,
Nick Bostrom joined

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:39.539
Stephen Hawking,
Max Tegmark, Elon

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:44.010
Musk, Lord Martin Rees,
Jan Tullin

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:46.612
and numerous
other AI researchers

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:48.715
in signing the Future of Life

00:05:48.748 --> 00:05:51.751
Institute's open
letter speaking to the

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:54.987
potential risks and
benefits associated

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:57.724
with artificial intelligence.

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:03.329
The signatories believe that
research on how to make AI

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:08.000
systems robust and beneficial
is both important and timely.

00:06:08.468 --> 00:06:11.170
And that there are
concrete research

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:13.906
directions that can
be pursued today.

00:06:15.108 --> 00:06:16.776
[intense ominous music]

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:21.347
[face paced dramatic music]

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:35.995
An autonomous car is a vehicle
that is capable of sensing

00:06:36.028 --> 00:06:39.565
its environment and
navigating without human input

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:43.035
and many such vehicles are being
developed.

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:45.037
But as of May 2017 automated

00:06:45.071 --> 00:06:47.473
cars permitted
on public roads are

00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:49.876
not yet fully autonomous.
They all

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:52.245
require a human
driver at the wheel

00:06:52.545 --> 00:06:56.582
who is ready at a moments notice
to take control of the vehicle.

00:06:57.717 --> 00:07:00.219
Among one of the
the main obstacles to

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:03.389
widespread adoption of
autonomous vehicles are

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:06.526
concerns about the
resulting loss of driving

00:07:06.559 --> 00:07:09.595
related jobs in the
road transport industry.

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:14.934
On March 18, 2018 the
first human was killed by an

00:07:14.967 --> 00:07:20.106
autonomous vehicle in Arizona
by an Uber self driving car.

00:07:21.908 --> 00:07:25.044
Self driving cars
combine a variety of

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:28.181
sensors to perceive
their surroundings,

00:07:28.214 --> 00:07:30.883
such as radar,
lidar, sonar, gps,

00:07:30.917 --> 00:07:34.320
odometry and inertial
measurement units.

00:07:34.854 --> 00:07:37.256
Advanced control
systems interpret

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:39.759
sensory information to identify

00:07:39.792 --> 00:07:42.462
appropriate
navigation paths as well

00:07:42.495 --> 00:07:45.164
as obstacles and
relevant signage.

00:07:46.098 --> 00:07:47.433
[tense music]

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:52.138
Connected vehicle platoons and

00:07:52.171 --> 00:07:54.440
long distance
trucking are seen as

00:07:54.474 --> 00:07:56.609
being at the
forefront of adopting

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:58.811
and implementing the technology.

00:08:00.546 --> 00:08:03.649
PC Magazine defines
a self driving car as a

00:08:03.683 --> 00:08:06.819
computer controlled
car that drives itself.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:10.323
The Union of Concerned
Scientists states

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:13.759
that self driving cars
are cars or trucks in

00:08:13.793 --> 00:08:16.929
which human drivers
are never required to

00:08:16.963 --> 00:08:20.132
take control to safely
operate the vehicle.

00:08:20.566 --> 00:08:24.704
Also known as autonomous
or driverless cars. They combine

00:08:24.737 --> 00:08:29.642
sensors and software to control,
navigate and drive the vehicle.

00:08:30.243 --> 00:08:31.444
[ominous music]

00:08:32.545 --> 00:08:35.047
Possible technological
obstacles for

00:08:35.081 --> 00:08:38.150
automated cars are
artificial intelligence

00:08:38.184 --> 00:08:40.920
is still not able to
properly function

00:08:40.953 --> 00:08:43.589
in chaotic inner
city environments.

00:08:44.423 --> 00:08:46.959
A car's computer
could potentially be

00:08:46.993 --> 00:08:49.462
compromised as
could a communication

00:08:49.495 --> 00:08:51.831
system between cars. A car could

00:08:51.864 --> 00:08:54.233
be hacked and
turned into a weapon.

00:08:55.301 --> 00:08:57.570
Susceptibility of
car sensing and

00:08:57.603 --> 00:09:00.540
navigation systems
to different types of

00:09:00.573 --> 00:09:02.975
weather such as
snow or deliberate

00:09:03.009 --> 00:09:06.312
interference,
included jamming and spoofing.

00:09:07.446 --> 00:09:09.949
Avoidance of large
animals requires

00:09:09.982 --> 00:09:12.985
recognition and
tracking and Volvo found

00:09:13.019 --> 00:09:15.555
that software suited to caribou,
deer

00:09:15.588 --> 00:09:18.591
and elk,
was ineffective with kangaroos.

00:09:19.358 --> 00:09:21.827
Autonomous cars
may require very high

00:09:21.861 --> 00:09:25.031
quality specialized
maps to operate properly.

00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:28.167
Were these maps may be
out of date they would need

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:31.070
to be able to fall back
to reasonable behaviors.

00:09:31.771 --> 00:09:32.838
[tense music]

00:09:33.339 --> 00:09:36.075
Competition for the
radio spectrum desired

00:09:36.108 --> 00:09:38.811
for the cars
communication is an issue.

00:09:39.579 --> 00:09:43.182
Field programmability for the
systems will require careful

00:09:43.215 --> 00:09:45.318
evaluation of
product development

00:09:45.351 --> 00:09:47.486
and the component supply chain

00:09:48.154 --> 00:09:51.057
and current road
infrastructure may need

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:54.794
changes for automated
cars to function optimally.

00:09:56.295 --> 00:09:59.198
One may bring up the adage:
"Just because you can

00:09:59.231 --> 00:10:02.134
do a thing doesn't mean
that you should do a thing."

00:10:02.768 --> 00:10:07.139
People are wary of self driving
cars and often don't trust them.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:11.844
Due to this and technology
factors, we may be a long way

00:10:11.877 --> 00:10:16.215
off from seeing a day
when all cars are self driving.

00:10:21.253 --> 00:10:22.388
[upbeat music]

00:10:28.728 --> 00:10:33.299
In science fiction we often see
the use of nanotechnology.

00:10:33.666 --> 00:10:36.335
Tiny robots that can
enter the body and

00:10:36.369 --> 00:10:39.672
repair cells or accomplish
cures to a disease.

00:10:40.039 --> 00:10:42.408
But nano particles
have been around

00:10:42.441 --> 00:10:45.144
since the 50's and
recent advancements

00:10:45.177 --> 00:10:49.815
makes this something we will see
more of today and in the future.

00:10:50.349 --> 00:10:53.986
There are several dangers with
this kind of technology, though.

00:10:55.488 --> 00:10:57.356
Nano particles are likely to be

00:10:57.390 --> 00:10:59.725
dangerous for
three main reasons.

00:11:00.526 --> 00:11:02.795
Nano particles may damage the
lungs.

00:11:03.162 --> 00:11:05.031
We know that the ultra fine

00:11:05.064 --> 00:11:07.600
particles from diesel machines,
power

00:11:07.633 --> 00:11:10.036
plants and
incinerators can cause

00:11:10.069 --> 00:11:12.438
considerable damage
to human lungs.

00:11:13.072 --> 00:11:15.808
This is both because
of their size as they

00:11:15.841 --> 00:11:18.544
can get deep
into the lungs, and also

00:11:18.577 --> 00:11:21.447
because they carry
other chemicals including

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:24.016
metals and
hydrocarbons in with them.

00:11:26.018 --> 00:11:28.988
Nano particles can get
into the body through

00:11:29.021 --> 00:11:31.724
the skin,
lungs and digestive system.

00:11:31.757 --> 00:11:34.527
This may help create
free radicals which

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:37.797
can cause cell damage
and damage to the DNA.

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:41.934
There's also concern that
once nano particles are in the

00:11:41.967 --> 00:11:46.138
bloodstream they'll be able to
cross the blood-brain barrier.

00:11:47.339 --> 00:11:50.810
The human body has
developed a tolerance to most

00:11:50.843 --> 00:11:54.313
naturally occurring elements
and molecules that it

00:11:54.346 --> 00:11:58.017
has contact with. It has
no natural immunity to new

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:01.721
substances and is more
likely to find them toxic.

00:12:03.289 --> 00:12:05.458
There's also the introduction of

00:12:05.491 --> 00:12:07.560
nano particles
or technology that

00:12:07.593 --> 00:12:10.062
could be injected
into person allowing

00:12:10.096 --> 00:12:12.331
other technologies
to track them.

00:12:12.865 --> 00:12:16.469
These particles can also be
sprayed or introduced into the

00:12:16.502 --> 00:12:18.738
environment on
the battle field to

00:12:18.771 --> 00:12:21.006
track whole armies,
or attack them.

00:12:21.707 --> 00:12:25.745
The particles then may harm
anyone in that environment.

00:12:28.781 --> 00:12:30.950
Though there are
positive uses for

00:12:30.983 --> 00:12:33.986
nanotechnology such
as in the medical field,

00:12:34.019 --> 00:12:36.722
the introduction of
any foreign technology

00:12:36.756 --> 00:12:39.291
into the body can
be very dangerous.

00:12:41.327 --> 00:12:45.064
Vaccines with nanotechnology
may attack a virus but

00:12:45.097 --> 00:12:49.201
also harm healthy cells
within the body or may be used

00:12:49.235 --> 00:12:53.139
to track the individual who
accepted the vaccine that

00:12:53.172 --> 00:12:57.109
can be triggered to make
you get sick, even kill you.

00:12:59.812 --> 00:13:03.182
Nanotechnology is already
a huge industry with billions

00:13:03.215 --> 00:13:06.385
of dollars being spent on
research and development

00:13:06.418 --> 00:13:09.622
worldwide. There's still a
great deal to learn about

00:13:09.655 --> 00:13:13.325
both the potential benefits
and risks of the technology.

00:13:13.893 --> 00:13:17.897
Nevertheless, most
experts agree that the use of

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:21.934
nano technology in electronics,
the pharmaceutical

00:13:21.967 --> 00:13:25.971
industry and in areas
such as medical imaging is

00:13:26.005 --> 00:13:30.142
outstripping our
understanding of the OHS risks.

00:13:30.176 --> 00:13:33.345
Nano technology
could lead to significant

00:13:33.379 --> 00:13:36.582
developments in medicine,
manufacturing

00:13:36.615 --> 00:13:39.318
and computing.
However it may also

00:13:39.351 --> 00:13:42.454
bring significant
new health hazards.

00:13:42.955 --> 00:13:44.623
[disconcerting music]

00:13:45.925 --> 00:13:46.992
[tense music]

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:56.936
Tracking American
citizens has become

00:13:56.969 --> 00:13:59.104
a major issue in the past decade

00:13:59.138 --> 00:14:01.207
with the emergence
of drones both

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:03.642
in the military and
corporate world.

00:14:04.076 --> 00:14:08.180
At almost any given time,
wherever you are it is likely a

00:14:08.214 --> 00:14:12.351
camera is recording your
movements, especially in a city.

00:14:14.253 --> 00:14:17.156
The combination of
surveillance drones and

00:14:17.189 --> 00:14:20.559
facial recognition has
made this much easier.

00:14:21.227 --> 00:14:24.063
Even commercial toy
drones have the ability

00:14:24.096 --> 00:14:26.765
to follow you simply
by looking at you.

00:14:27.333 --> 00:14:29.101
Drones have been used to

00:14:29.134 --> 00:14:31.604
intentionally cause harm.
It's the most

00:14:31.637 --> 00:14:34.773
dangerous because they're
the bad actors that have

00:14:34.807 --> 00:14:36.809
nefarious intentions.

00:14:37.543 --> 00:14:40.012
Drones are being
used for illicit

00:14:40.045 --> 00:14:42.548
activities which include but are

00:14:42.581 --> 00:14:45.251
not limited to
transport of illegal

00:14:45.284 --> 00:14:47.920
drugs,
dropping leaflets into NFL

00:14:47.953 --> 00:14:50.556
stadiums,
dropping contraband such

00:14:50.589 --> 00:14:53.225
as drugs, cell phones,
cigarettes

00:14:53.259 --> 00:14:55.861
and weapons into prison yards.
And

00:14:55.895 --> 00:14:58.464
in some cases carrying weapons.

00:14:59.565 --> 00:15:01.834
In one case a drone
helped an inmate

00:15:01.867 --> 00:15:04.103
escape from a
correctional facility.

00:15:06.639 --> 00:15:09.942
To further validate
concerns the US military has

00:15:09.975 --> 00:15:13.646
identified a number of
ways that commercial off the

00:15:13.679 --> 00:15:17.383
shelf drones have been
weaponized with intentions to

00:15:17.416 --> 00:15:21.120
attack US war fighters or
military bases over seas.

00:15:22.621 --> 00:15:26.258
There are two other
complications when it comes to

00:15:26.292 --> 00:15:29.828
addressing potential
drone threats. First, there's

00:15:29.862 --> 00:15:33.365
a combination of 21
federal rules and regulations

00:15:33.399 --> 00:15:36.902
prohibiting the use of
counter drone technology.

00:15:36.936 --> 00:15:40.239
The second issue is
that, until recently, drones

00:15:40.272 --> 00:15:43.943
were not required to be
registered and there is a

00:15:43.976 --> 00:15:47.446
large number of unregistered
drones which make it

00:15:47.479 --> 00:15:50.950
extremely difficult to
identify the drone pilot.

00:15:51.717 --> 00:15:54.653
This is especially
important to identify

00:15:54.687 --> 00:15:57.656
friend from foe.
Additionally there is

00:15:57.690 --> 00:16:00.926
no single counter drone
technology that addresses

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:03.729
all the various
drone technologies.

00:16:04.096 --> 00:16:06.832
One obvious consideration
is understanding

00:16:06.865 --> 00:16:09.034
the implications of taking down

00:16:09.068 --> 00:16:11.503
a drone while flying
over people and

00:16:11.537 --> 00:16:13.973
the possible injury
to those people.

00:16:16.208 --> 00:16:19.144
Drones can also be
used to spy on you and

00:16:19.178 --> 00:16:22.114
combined with other
technologies such as

00:16:22.147 --> 00:16:25.084
listening devices
and IR scanners, they

00:16:25.117 --> 00:16:28.087
can watch you and
record your movements.

00:16:29.655 --> 00:16:33.225
Every new technology
comes with the possibility of

00:16:33.258 --> 00:16:36.795
being used for undesirable
or dangerous purposes.

00:16:37.329 --> 00:16:40.699
The future of drones
will require a balance of

00:16:40.733 --> 00:16:44.103
enabling drones for good,
countering drones for

00:16:44.136 --> 00:16:47.840
bad and a comprehensive air
traffic management system

00:16:47.873 --> 00:16:51.343
that encompasses manned
and unmanned aircraft.

00:16:52.211 --> 00:16:53.479
[dramatic music]

00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:02.554
[upbeat music]

00:17:09.995 --> 00:17:13.565
Protesters in Hong Kong
are taking extraordinary

00:17:13.599 --> 00:17:16.468
measures to protect
their identities.

00:17:16.769 --> 00:17:19.171
That's because
facial recognition

00:17:19.204 --> 00:17:21.640
technologies in China have been

00:17:21.673 --> 00:17:24.276
used to surveil
and detain people

00:17:24.309 --> 00:17:26.912
suspected of
crimes in the region.

00:17:27.679 --> 00:17:30.716
Having their faces being
recognized by cameras

00:17:30.749 --> 00:17:34.253
could have devastating
consequences for protesters.

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:37.489
These protesters
are using various

00:17:37.523 --> 00:17:40.692
techniques to throw
off facial recognition

00:17:40.726 --> 00:17:43.295
cameras,
including lasers that the

00:17:43.328 --> 00:17:45.898
cameras can't
process or recognize.

00:17:46.398 --> 00:17:49.001
Full coverage gas
masks and ear wear.

00:17:49.034 --> 00:17:51.503
They have put up
umbrellas around

00:17:51.537 --> 00:17:54.073
cameras to block
them and even torn

00:17:54.106 --> 00:17:56.508
down facial recognition towers.

00:17:58.677 --> 00:18:00.145
Facial recognition is a

00:18:00.179 --> 00:18:02.314
polarizing topic
and is sometimes

00:18:02.347 --> 00:18:04.450
seen as a problematic
development

00:18:04.483 --> 00:18:06.351
in surveillance capitalism.

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:10.389
People generally don't give

00:18:10.422 --> 00:18:12.991
permission or even
know they're being

00:18:13.025 --> 00:18:17.563
tracked. They also don't know
how their faces are being used.

00:18:19.431 --> 00:18:22.935
For example, when you
walk into most retail stores

00:18:22.968 --> 00:18:26.472
there is a security camera
there to ward off theft.

00:18:26.939 --> 00:18:31.443
However, that camera could be
doing much more than warding

00:18:31.477 --> 00:18:35.948
off theft. It could use your
face for other databases so

00:18:35.981 --> 00:18:40.252
the store can market to you
and build a behavior profile

00:18:40.285 --> 00:18:42.788
that links your
in-store activity

00:18:42.821 --> 00:18:44.990
with your online activity.

00:18:47.559 --> 00:18:51.530
Think about how Amazon
built its facial recognition

00:18:51.563 --> 00:18:56.535
technology. It curated photos
of your online profiles and your

00:18:56.568 --> 00:19:01.073
shopping experiences as well
as images from its Ring Doorbell

00:19:01.106 --> 00:19:06.011
security application and
put together a profile of you.

00:19:07.246 --> 00:19:10.549
So is security worth giving up
your privacy?

00:19:11.116 --> 00:19:13.785
The problem is that
facial recognition

00:19:13.819 --> 00:19:17.222
software is calibrated
to white men, therefore

00:19:17.256 --> 00:19:19.925
it misidentifies
people of color and

00:19:19.958 --> 00:19:23.328
especially women of
color at alarming rates.

00:19:23.762 --> 00:19:26.632
Increasing the risk
that certain groups

00:19:26.665 --> 00:19:30.035
will be incorrectly
associated with crimes.

00:19:32.571 --> 00:19:35.240
Currently there
are no transparent

00:19:35.274 --> 00:19:38.644
rules on how facial
recognition data can

00:19:38.677 --> 00:19:41.480
be used and how
it can be shared. In

00:19:41.513 --> 00:19:44.716
some cases it has
been ruled as lawful.

00:19:45.284 --> 00:19:49.021
It's a lot to hand over your
face to unlimited entities

00:19:49.054 --> 00:19:52.891
who have not figured out
the rules for using that data.

00:19:54.393 --> 00:19:58.063
We may never reach the
place where our faces determine

00:19:58.096 --> 00:20:01.767
our social standing,
as is the case in Hong Kong but

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:05.704
will it determine our credit
ratings? Our job prospects?

00:20:06.171 --> 00:20:10.075
These are degrees of invasion
that are still possible.

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:14.112
It's time to protect
your privacy

00:20:14.146 --> 00:20:16.648
like you were
protesting against an

00:20:16.682 --> 00:20:19.051
authoritarian government.
Think of

00:20:19.084 --> 00:20:21.386
it as if your life
and the lives of

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:23.755
your family and
friends depends on

00:20:23.789 --> 00:20:26.191
it.
Not to suggest you walk around

00:20:26.225 --> 00:20:28.427
with masks on all
day but be more

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:30.996
diligent about what
you post online.

00:20:33.565 --> 00:20:35.734
Share photos and
videos of family

00:20:35.767 --> 00:20:37.970
and friends on a secure network,

00:20:38.003 --> 00:20:40.472
understand that
when you buy personal

00:20:40.505 --> 00:20:42.941
assistant devices
you're giving up

00:20:42.975 --> 00:20:45.143
intimate details
about your self,

00:20:45.177 --> 00:20:47.779
your family and your friends,
and you

00:20:47.813 --> 00:20:50.048
have no transparency
on how those

00:20:50.082 --> 00:20:53.085
intimate details are
being shared or used.

00:20:53.619 --> 00:20:56.388
Put covers on your
device cameras and only

00:20:56.421 --> 00:20:59.258
uncover them when
you're using the camera.

00:20:59.758 --> 00:21:03.395
You can't stop cameras
from picking up your face and

00:21:03.428 --> 00:21:07.099
storing it but you can take
control whenever possible.

00:21:08.834 --> 00:21:12.638
Businesses and organizations
also have an obligation

00:21:12.671 --> 00:21:16.475
to their users and customers
to protect their rights.

00:21:17.476 --> 00:21:20.946
Privacy is one of those
fundamental rights, one that we

00:21:20.979 --> 00:21:23.081
should enjoy in
our digital world

00:21:23.115 --> 00:21:25.017
as well as in our physical one.

00:21:26.485 --> 00:21:29.888
Without the protection
of those rights around

00:21:29.921 --> 00:21:33.425
technology like facial
recognition, we may end

00:21:33.458 --> 00:21:36.995
up in a place both as
businesses and individuals

00:21:37.029 --> 00:21:40.365
where there is no
escape from surveillance

00:21:40.966 --> 00:21:43.168
and that sort of
dystopia is not the

00:21:43.201 --> 00:21:45.370
world we
want to live in.

00:21:45.804 --> 00:21:46.905
[upbeat music]

00:21:47.806 --> 00:21:50.142
There should be
more regulation around

00:21:50.175 --> 00:21:52.911
facial recognition
and both as individuals

00:21:52.944 --> 00:21:55.447
and organizations
we should be fighting

00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:58.483
against improper usage
of facial recognition.

00:21:58.917 --> 00:22:01.653
Get behind some of
the facial recognition

00:22:01.687 --> 00:22:05.023
legislation that is being
proposed. One example

00:22:05.057 --> 00:22:08.160
is the Commercial
Facial Recognition Privacy

00:22:08.193 --> 00:22:11.129
Act of 2019,
proposed in Washington, DC.

00:22:11.596 --> 00:22:14.933
In which would prohibit
commercial users of

00:22:14.966 --> 00:22:18.303
facial recognition
technology from collecting

00:22:18.337 --> 00:22:21.139
and re-sharing data
for identifying or

00:22:21.173 --> 00:22:24.443
tracking customers
without their consent.

00:22:25.877 --> 00:22:27.979
Microsoft president
Brad Smith has

00:22:28.013 --> 00:22:30.115
spoken out in
support of the bill.

00:22:31.650 --> 00:22:34.086
In the meantime, in the absence

00:22:34.119 --> 00:22:36.588
of solid laws,
opt for privacy and

00:22:36.621 --> 00:22:39.057
be transparent about the way

00:22:39.091 --> 00:22:42.060
you allow
the use of your data.

00:22:43.595 --> 00:22:44.930
[upbeat music]

00:22:48.166 --> 00:22:50.635
[disconcerting music]

00:23:00.379 --> 00:23:02.047
Have you been chipped?

00:23:02.414 --> 00:23:06.585
Implementing chips in
humans has privacy and security

00:23:06.618 --> 00:23:11.390
implications that go well
beyond cameras in public places.

00:23:11.857 --> 00:23:14.593
Facial recognition, tracking of

00:23:14.626 --> 00:23:17.295
our locations,
our driving habits,

00:23:17.329 --> 00:23:22.401
our spending histories and even
beyond ownership of your data.

00:23:23.335 --> 00:23:25.604
This topic touches
upon your hand, your

00:23:25.637 --> 00:23:29.374
heart, your brain and the
rest of your body. Literally.

00:23:31.042 --> 00:23:34.679
This new development is
set to give a very different

00:23:34.713 --> 00:23:37.849
meaning to hacking
the body or bio hacking.

00:23:38.583 --> 00:23:40.952
While cyber experts
continue to worry

00:23:40.986 --> 00:23:43.755
about protecting
critical infrastructure

00:23:43.789 --> 00:23:46.658
and mitigating
security risks that could

00:23:46.691 --> 00:23:49.494
harm the economy
or cause a loss of life.

00:23:50.395 --> 00:23:54.065
Implanted chips also
effect health but add in new

00:23:54.099 --> 00:23:58.537
dimensions that conflict
with people's religious beliefs.

00:24:00.305 --> 00:24:05.110
RFID microchips embedded under
the skin with a procedure

00:24:05.143 --> 00:24:07.379
that's already
cheap and available,

00:24:07.412 --> 00:24:09.614
provide a digital
interface to the

00:24:09.648 --> 00:24:12.417
real world,
centered about the holders

00:24:12.651 --> 00:24:15.454
identity,
credit card information,

00:24:15.487 --> 00:24:18.557
bus pass,
library card and many other

00:24:18.590 --> 00:24:20.759
sources of information
you currently

00:24:20.792 --> 00:24:23.428
carry in your purse or wallet.

00:24:23.628 --> 00:24:28.900
And it can instead be stored on
an RFID chip under your skin.

00:24:29.301 --> 00:24:31.102
[disconcerting sounds]

00:24:31.136 --> 00:24:34.372
However getting chipped
could be a way to control

00:24:34.406 --> 00:24:38.109
you. When guns are paired
to the chips in their owners,

00:24:38.143 --> 00:24:41.546
revolutionary heroes can
no longer break into their

00:24:41.580 --> 00:24:45.517
oppressors arsenal to turn
their firepower against them.

00:24:47.686 --> 00:24:50.388
Putting so much
importance on a device

00:24:50.422 --> 00:24:52.958
only available
to those that seek

00:24:52.991 --> 00:24:55.627
it out requires
keeping close tabs on

00:24:55.660 --> 00:24:58.263
its availability
and affordability.

00:24:59.297 --> 00:25:03.401
If the advantages effectively
disadvantage those who

00:25:03.435 --> 00:25:08.206
choose not to participate,
gaps between classes may widen.

00:25:10.675 --> 00:25:13.445
In a world controlled
entirely by chips

00:25:13.478 --> 00:25:16.648
within your skin,
its possible that hackers

00:25:16.681 --> 00:25:19.551
and evil doers could
scan and replicate

00:25:19.584 --> 00:25:22.487
the data on your
chips onto their own,

00:25:22.888 --> 00:25:26.391
effectively replacing your
physical presence which is

00:25:26.424 --> 00:25:30.428
notably different from just
stealing digital credentials.

00:25:31.630 --> 00:25:34.599
Every Hollywood
movie has taught us that

00:25:34.633 --> 00:25:37.636
implanted microchips
are primarily for big

00:25:37.669 --> 00:25:40.639
brother,
governments and corporations to

00:25:40.672 --> 00:25:43.642
continuously track
our every whereabouts.

00:25:44.109 --> 00:25:47.913
This is a real concern that
needs to be handled with privacy

00:25:47.946 --> 00:25:51.449
controls and good security
practices from the get go.

00:25:53.485 --> 00:25:55.921
In a world where you
purchase food with

00:25:55.954 --> 00:25:58.256
a chip in your
hand, it's not hard to

00:25:58.290 --> 00:26:00.559
think that some
people might prefer

00:26:00.592 --> 00:26:03.128
to use a card in
their wallet instead.

00:26:03.695 --> 00:26:07.465
However, it's also not hard to
imagine a world in which

00:26:07.499 --> 00:26:11.303
the benefits of a microchip
mandate its usage.

00:26:11.636 --> 00:26:14.973
Basically requiring
everyone to receive a

00:26:15.006 --> 00:26:18.977
microchip, or starve,
lose their job, etcetera.

00:26:19.277 --> 00:26:20.478
[ominous music]

00:26:21.246 --> 00:26:23.582
One of the benefits
of a microchip is

00:26:23.615 --> 00:26:25.951
it's invisible to those
who don't know

00:26:25.984 --> 00:26:28.520
about it. Making it
harder for thieves and

00:26:28.553 --> 00:26:31.056
adversaries to steal
your information.

00:26:31.756 --> 00:26:35.093
However this advantage
is a double edged sword

00:26:35.126 --> 00:26:38.430
when you consider that
people could potentially

00:26:38.463 --> 00:26:41.499
be oblivious to microchips,
implanted by others

00:26:41.533 --> 00:26:44.569
in themselves while
sleeping or unconscious.

00:26:45.036 --> 00:26:46.771
[tense upbeat music]

00:26:46.805 --> 00:26:50.609
Biblical apocalyptics
claim it could be the mark of

00:26:50.642 --> 00:26:54.479
the beast indicating the
beginning of revelations.

00:26:57.048 --> 00:27:00.352
There is currently no
government agency that

00:27:00.385 --> 00:27:03.455
oversees or controls
neuro-electric interface

00:27:03.488 --> 00:27:05.824
enhancements, with the
closest body

00:27:05.857 --> 00:27:07.659
being the FDA due to

00:27:07.692 --> 00:27:11.096
its broad jurisdiction
over medical devices.

00:27:11.997 --> 00:27:15.900
The long term health risks
of implanting microchips

00:27:15.934 --> 00:27:19.471
in humans is relatively unknown.
On one hand

00:27:19.504 --> 00:27:22.774
human micro chipping
has been green lighted

00:27:22.807 --> 00:27:26.711
around the world by
various authoritative

00:27:26.745 --> 00:27:30.482
bodies,
including the FDA in America.

00:27:31.282 --> 00:27:32.884
[tense upbeat music]

00:27:39.224 --> 00:27:40.959
[upbeat tribal drum beat]

00:27:48.800 --> 00:27:51.002
It may seem we live in a science

00:27:51.036 --> 00:27:53.738
fiction world,
after all we have a space

00:27:53.772 --> 00:27:56.041
station in orbit.
We've been to the

00:27:56.074 --> 00:27:58.710
moon and new
advanced satellites bring

00:27:58.743 --> 00:28:01.179
us information from
around the planet.

00:28:01.212 --> 00:28:03.648
But that world
could turn out to be

00:28:03.682 --> 00:28:06.184
a dystopian empire
where the population

00:28:06.217 --> 00:28:08.586
is controlled and
herded in line.

00:28:09.821 --> 00:28:14.359
At the conclusion of the
June 1992 United Nations

00:28:14.392 --> 00:28:20.031
Conference on Environment and
Development in Rio de Janeiro,

00:28:20.065 --> 00:28:25.136
Brazil. President George H.
W. Bush and the leaders of

00:28:25.170 --> 00:28:30.375
177 other nations signed a
document known as agenda 21.

00:28:30.408 --> 00:28:33.545
At the time it was seen
as a perfectly sensible

00:28:33.578 --> 00:28:36.514
planning paper.
A non-binding statement

00:28:36.548 --> 00:28:39.884
of intent aimed at
dealing with sustainability

00:28:39.918 --> 00:28:42.554
on an increasingly
crowded planet.

00:28:43.588 --> 00:28:46.357
But
in the 22 years since that day,

00:28:46.391 --> 00:28:48.526
at the hands of
groups like the John

00:28:48.560 --> 00:28:51.963
Birch society,
Agent 21 has been

00:28:51.996 --> 00:28:54.699
transformed in
much of the American

00:28:54.733 --> 00:28:57.335
public's mind into
a secret plot to

00:28:57.368 --> 00:29:00.438
impose a totalitarian
world government.

00:29:00.472 --> 00:29:03.108
A nefarious effort
to crush freedom

00:29:03.141 --> 00:29:05.777
in the name of environmentalism.

00:29:08.079 --> 00:29:11.916
Some say Agenda 21 will
lead to a new Dark Ages

00:29:11.950 --> 00:29:15.754
of pain and misery yet
unknown to mankind. It is

00:29:15.787 --> 00:29:19.624
a comprehensive plan of
utopian environmentalism,

00:29:19.657 --> 00:29:23.561
social engineering and
global political control.

00:29:23.995 --> 00:29:27.465
The most dangerous threat
to America's sovereignty

00:29:27.499 --> 00:29:30.468
yet and technology
will make it possible.

00:29:31.436 --> 00:29:34.939
It will make our nation
a vassal of the UN,

00:29:34.973 --> 00:29:38.476
result in the destruction
of our lives, force

00:29:38.510 --> 00:29:42.013
rural areas,
populations to be decimated and

00:29:42.046 --> 00:29:44.415
lead to having 90% of the

00:29:44.449 --> 00:29:47.685
population murdered.
The end these

00:29:47.719 --> 00:29:52.257
critics all agree will be the
imposition of a collectivist

00:29:52.290 --> 00:29:54.292
world government.

00:29:55.193 --> 00:29:59.130
Several politicians are
aware of the agenda with

00:29:59.164 --> 00:30:01.566
state and local authorities
passing legislation

00:30:01.599 --> 00:30:04.969
to ban it. The list of
fears include one-world

00:30:05.003 --> 00:30:09.741
currency, one religion if any,
one military, no

00:30:09.774 --> 00:30:14.779
private property,
no family units, mandatory

00:30:14.813 --> 00:30:18.917
vaccines, microchips
for everyone, social credit

00:30:18.950 --> 00:30:23.021
systems, 5G monitoring
and the government raising

00:30:23.054 --> 00:30:27.125
your children and
controlling all the schools.

00:30:27.525 --> 00:30:32.463
People would not be able to own
cars or businesses as everything

00:30:32.497 --> 00:30:36.768
will be managed either by
corporations or governments.

00:30:38.970 --> 00:30:40.471
[upbeat disconcerting music]

00:30:50.815 --> 00:30:53.785
In an Agenda 21 world
you would have to be

00:30:53.818 --> 00:30:56.855
micro chipped so the
technology could track

00:30:56.888 --> 00:30:59.891
you. What you buy
and where you go would

00:30:59.924 --> 00:31:03.027
depend on your
compliance with the agenda.

00:31:03.895 --> 00:31:06.431
Technology would
track your every

00:31:06.464 --> 00:31:08.833
move with facial recognition,

00:31:08.867 --> 00:31:13.638
microchips, drones and other
sophisticated tracing science.

00:31:14.639 --> 00:31:19.310
All of the technology needed
to do this is already in play

00:31:19.344 --> 00:31:24.015
now with more new technologies
being developed every year.

00:31:24.716 --> 00:31:27.619
We are all moving
toward a one-world

00:31:27.652 --> 00:31:31.389
government faster than
previously predicted.

00:31:32.824 --> 00:31:35.793
The increasing use of
drones for commercial

00:31:35.827 --> 00:31:39.097
purposes has become
one of the biggest emerging

00:31:39.130 --> 00:31:42.467
threats to the future of
airplane safety according

00:31:42.500 --> 00:31:45.370
to Allianz Global
Corporate and Specialty.

00:31:45.937 --> 00:31:49.474
The expected rise in the
use of drones or unmanned

00:31:49.507 --> 00:31:53.645
aerial vehicles for a host
of different applications may

00:31:53.678 --> 00:31:57.515
leave operators exposed
to a whole new set of risks

00:31:57.548 --> 00:32:01.419
including third party
damage or injury and liability.

00:32:03.655 --> 00:32:06.424
One of the biggest risks, it
said, was

00:32:06.457 --> 00:32:08.726
from radio frequency
interference

00:32:08.760 --> 00:32:13.731
resulting in loss of control and
in worse case scenario,

00:32:13.765 --> 00:32:15.900
fatalities.

00:32:15.934 --> 00:32:18.970
Other problems include
invasion or privacy,

00:32:19.003 --> 00:32:21.873
aerial surveillance
and data collection.

00:32:24.609 --> 00:32:27.812
Privacy advocates
contend that with drones, the

00:32:27.845 --> 00:32:31.049
government will be able
to engage in widespread

00:32:31.082 --> 00:32:34.419
pervasive surveillance
because drones are cheaper

00:32:34.452 --> 00:32:37.422
to operate than their
manned counterparts.

00:32:38.122 --> 00:32:40.925
Drones are being used
by law enforcement

00:32:40.959 --> 00:32:43.628
and border control surveillance
teams in case

00:32:43.661 --> 00:32:46.564
of essential supplies,
however, drones are

00:32:46.597 --> 00:32:49.500
not being used
exclusively by good guys.

00:32:52.070 --> 00:32:56.407
In case of natural disasters,
search and rescue teams employ

00:32:56.441 --> 00:33:00.778
them to gather information,
or to drop essential supplies.

00:33:01.279 --> 00:33:06.351
However, drones are not being
used exclusively by good guys.

00:33:07.018 --> 00:33:09.854
Bad guys are leveraging
drones to achieve

00:33:09.887 --> 00:33:12.657
their malicious objectives,
being

00:33:12.690 --> 00:33:15.293
easy to control, drones can be

00:33:15.326 --> 00:33:18.196
used to perform
different attacks.

00:33:20.231 --> 00:33:22.900
The reliance on
wireless communications

00:33:22.934 --> 00:33:25.303
make drones
vulnerable to various

00:33:25.336 --> 00:33:27.572
attacks. These attacks can have

00:33:27.605 --> 00:33:30.208
drastic effects
including commercial

00:33:30.241 --> 00:33:32.710
and non-commercial losses.
In this

00:33:32.744 --> 00:33:35.213
context there is
a lack of proper

00:33:35.246 --> 00:33:37.715
understanding on
how hackers perform

00:33:37.749 --> 00:33:40.184
their attacks and
hijack a drone

00:33:40.651 --> 00:33:43.855
in order to intercept
it or even crash it. In

00:33:43.888 --> 00:33:47.592
fact, drones can also be
compromised for malicious

00:33:47.625 --> 00:33:50.928
purposes hence there
is a need to detect them

00:33:50.962 --> 00:33:54.132
and prevent them from
causing any damage.

00:33:55.900 --> 00:33:59.904
With a drone you could be
followed anywhere and tracked,

00:33:59.937 --> 00:34:03.541
military drones are already
being deployed on the

00:34:03.574 --> 00:34:07.111
battlefield for surveillance.
It would be a simple

00:34:07.145 --> 00:34:11.182
step to bring them home
and use them to track citizens.

00:34:14.252 --> 00:34:18.423
In August of 2018 a drone
led assassination attempt was

00:34:18.456 --> 00:34:22.727
foiled when two drones wrapped
with explosives were used

00:34:22.760 --> 00:34:26.731
to assassinate the Venezuelan
President. They were shot

00:34:26.764 --> 00:34:31.169
down by snipers, injuring
eight soldiers and one civilian.

00:34:32.336 --> 00:34:34.372
Actually, drones
are being used by

00:34:34.405 --> 00:34:36.441
insurgents and terrorists alike.

00:34:37.375 --> 00:34:40.211
Drones were used by ISIS to drop

00:34:40.244 --> 00:34:43.081
bombs and to film
propaganda videos in

00:34:43.114 --> 00:34:46.317
conflict zones such
as the targeting

00:34:46.350 --> 00:34:49.620
of Iraq and Syrian
military personnel.

00:34:51.055 --> 00:34:54.659
Being quiet and performing
at altitude, you would

00:34:54.692 --> 00:34:58.296
never know if you were
being observed by a drone.

00:34:59.130 --> 00:35:02.500
Justification for
surveillance of citizens

00:35:02.533 --> 00:35:05.937
are in court cases
now around the country.

00:35:06.737 --> 00:35:08.339
[tense somber music]

00:35:17.849 --> 00:35:19.650
[upbeat high pitched music]

00:35:31.629 --> 00:35:34.899
Many futuristic weapons
are already being

00:35:34.932 --> 00:35:38.202
used on the battlefield today.
The military

00:35:38.236 --> 00:35:41.105
is always poised for
advanced weapons

00:35:41.139 --> 00:35:44.575
systems and developing
new weapons yearly.

00:35:48.112 --> 00:35:50.548
The XM-25 grenade launcher is

00:35:50.581 --> 00:35:53.684
equipped with a laser
range finder and

00:35:53.718 --> 00:35:56.154
on board computer. It packs a

00:35:56.187 --> 00:35:59.323
magazine of four
25mm projectiles and

00:35:59.357 --> 00:36:02.260
programs them
to detonate as they

00:36:02.293 --> 00:36:05.129
pass by their targets.
That feature

00:36:05.163 --> 00:36:07.632
will allow soldiers to strike

00:36:07.665 --> 00:36:10.668
enemies who
are taking cover.

00:36:11.202 --> 00:36:15.406
By 2012 the army has armed
every infantry squad and

00:36:15.439 --> 00:36:20.111
special forces unit with at
least one of the big guns.

00:36:21.779 --> 00:36:24.882
In August a lucky
soldier got to pull

00:36:24.916 --> 00:36:28.019
the trigger and fire
off an HEAB high

00:36:28.052 --> 00:36:31.422
explosive air burst
round at the Aberdeen

00:36:31.455 --> 00:36:34.358
testing ground in Maryland.
Those

00:36:34.392 --> 00:36:37.361
projectiles pack quiet a punch.
They

00:36:37.395 --> 00:36:40.798
were purposely 300%
more effective than

00:36:40.831 --> 00:36:44.035
normal ammo and
will be able to strike

00:36:44.068 --> 00:36:47.004
targets as far as
2300 feet away.

00:36:48.906 --> 00:36:53.678
Remotely operated weapons are
showing up everywhere. Israel is

00:36:53.711 --> 00:36:56.314
building an automated kill zone.

00:36:56.347 --> 00:36:58.916
An American firm,
Moore Industries,

00:36:58.950 --> 00:37:01.452
offers turret that can aim and

00:37:01.485 --> 00:37:03.988
fire two automatic shotguns.
Some

00:37:04.021 --> 00:37:06.757
robots have been
defusing bombs for

00:37:06.791 --> 00:37:09.594
years but none have seen combat.

00:37:10.561 --> 00:37:15.199
According to Lieutenant General
Rick Lynch who believes that 122

00:37:15.233 --> 00:37:19.937
men could have been spared if
combat robots had been working.

00:37:21.973 --> 00:37:26.344
There was a set of armed robots
sent to Iraq. They never fired

00:37:26.377 --> 00:37:28.346
a shot, however. They weren't

00:37:28.379 --> 00:37:30.748
allowed to.
No one could guarantee

00:37:30.781 --> 00:37:33.251
that the robots
wouldn't go berserk

00:37:33.284 --> 00:37:35.386
and mow down friendly troops

00:37:35.419 --> 00:37:37.455
or otherwise malfunction even

00:37:37.488 --> 00:37:40.057
though they have
lots of safeguards.

00:37:41.892 --> 00:37:46.163
Considering how much
firepower they pack, safeguards

00:37:46.197 --> 00:37:49.967
are really important.
The MARS system can be

00:37:50.001 --> 00:37:52.837
equipped with four grenade
launchers and a machine

00:37:52.870 --> 00:37:58.743
gun that packs 400 rounds
of 7.62 caliber ammunition.

00:38:03.614 --> 00:38:05.950
But it's manufacturers like to

00:38:05.983 --> 00:38:08.819
point out its less
lethal capabilities.

00:38:08.853 --> 00:38:11.455
Instead of mowing
people down, it

00:38:11.489 --> 00:38:14.091
can stick to the
fine print of the

00:38:14.125 --> 00:38:15.726
first law of
robotics and fire tear

00:38:15.760 --> 00:38:18.362
gas canisters,
smoke grenades, smoke

00:38:18.396 --> 00:38:21.832
bombs and perhaps
even tasers upcoming

00:38:21.866 --> 00:38:25.303
40mm people zapper projectile.

00:38:26.737 --> 00:38:29.540
Three were deployed in Iraq last
year.

00:38:31.309 --> 00:38:34.111
The active denial
system fires a beam

00:38:34.145 --> 00:38:36.981
of millimeter wave radiation.
It makes

00:38:37.014 --> 00:38:39.784
people feel like
their skin is burning

00:38:39.817 --> 00:38:42.620
without causing any
permanent damage.

00:38:43.921 --> 00:38:46.724
Though promising as
a nonlethal weapon,

00:38:46.757 --> 00:38:49.627
the pain rate has
some serious limits.

00:38:50.494 --> 00:38:52.663
On a rainy day
water droplets will

00:38:52.697 --> 00:38:55.499
disperse the beam
and it may feel warm and

00:38:55.533 --> 00:38:58.102
refreshing instead
of frightening, on a

00:38:58.135 --> 00:39:01.038
hot day the cooling
system might give out.

00:39:01.072 --> 00:39:03.674
The problems don't stop there.
Ratheon's

00:39:03.708 --> 00:39:06.043
baby is bulky and
despite repeated

00:39:06.077 --> 00:39:08.779
requests to send it
into battle, shipments

00:39:08.813 --> 00:39:11.582
of the energy weapon
have been delayed.

00:39:12.083 --> 00:39:15.353
The military is looking for a
strong lighter weapon.

00:39:17.688 --> 00:39:19.056
[laid back music]

00:39:20.224 --> 00:39:24.495
If troops spot someone
suspicious approaching them,
they can

00:39:24.528 --> 00:39:26.597
use the long range acoustic

00:39:26.630 --> 00:39:29.133
device to send a
warning message.

00:39:29.567 --> 00:39:33.537
It fires narrow beams of
sound waves that can be heard

00:39:33.571 --> 00:39:37.975
clearly from about 1000 feet
away. Crank up the power and

00:39:38.008 --> 00:39:41.912
it can emit a warning tone
so loud that anyone in its

00:39:41.946 --> 00:39:46.417
path would have no choice
but to cover their ears and run.

00:39:49.286 --> 00:39:52.556
The manufacturer
doesn't like to call these

00:39:52.590 --> 00:39:55.926
devices weapons even
though they've been used

00:39:55.960 --> 00:39:59.163
to repel pirates.
Cops used them to harass

00:39:59.196 --> 00:40:02.400
protesters at the G20
summit in Pittsburgh.

00:40:04.068 --> 00:40:06.003
Drones are arguably the most

00:40:06.036 --> 00:40:08.406
controversial
weapon in the war on

00:40:08.439 --> 00:40:10.441
terror. By some accounts they

00:40:10.474 --> 00:40:12.777
are deeply feared
by the Taliban.

00:40:13.711 --> 00:40:16.247
They've taken out
Al-Qaeda and Taliban

00:40:16.280 --> 00:40:19.350
leaders and their sound
when flying low is a

00:40:19.383 --> 00:40:22.153
constant annoyance
and reminder of their

00:40:22.186 --> 00:40:25.423
menace. But they also
kill a lot of civilians.

00:40:26.657 --> 00:40:29.927
They are, however, far
more cost effective than

00:40:29.960 --> 00:40:33.798
supersonic fighter jets.
Predators can pack two Hell

00:40:33.831 --> 00:40:37.401
Fire missiles. Their big
brothers, Reapers, can hold

00:40:37.435 --> 00:40:40.905
four Hell Fires and up
to two 500 pound bombs.

00:40:41.739 --> 00:40:43.974
Flash bang grenades
were designed to stun

00:40:44.008 --> 00:40:46.744
people but they have a
pretty bad safety record.

00:40:46.777 --> 00:40:49.413
The little bombs have
dismembered at least one

00:40:49.447 --> 00:40:52.116
soldier and caused
hearing loss in others.

00:40:52.750 --> 00:40:56.720
To remedy that problem, Mark
Grubelich and his colleagues

00:40:56.754 --> 00:41:01.125
at Sandia National Laboratory
built the improved flash bang

00:41:01.158 --> 00:41:05.362
grenade. It hurls flaming
aluminum particles into the air

00:41:05.396 --> 00:41:09.567
causing a bright flash without
an accompanying shock wave.

00:41:11.402 --> 00:41:13.838
Even the angriest
mobs would probably

00:41:13.871 --> 00:41:16.240
think twice about
trying to pass a

00:41:16.273 --> 00:41:18.876
taser shock wave barrier.
It's the less

00:41:18.909 --> 00:41:21.512
lethal equivalent
of a claymore mine.

00:41:22.079 --> 00:41:26.317
Push the big red button
and it will fire 24 electrified

00:41:26.350 --> 00:41:30.087
probes at the same
time in a single direction.

00:41:31.288 --> 00:41:32.890
After learning about an

00:41:32.923 --> 00:41:35.259
experimental
weapon that can make

00:41:35.292 --> 00:41:37.328
people feel seasick, Limor Fried

00:41:37.361 --> 00:41:39.797
and Phil Torrone
more decided to

00:41:39.830 --> 00:41:43.834
build their own. They did it
for less than $250 dollars and

00:41:43.868 --> 00:41:48.305
wrote step by step instructions
so anyone can make one at home.

00:41:48.906 --> 00:41:54.612
It can cause a nauseating light
show with 36 pulsating LED's.

00:41:56.780 --> 00:41:59.116
Now if you're worried
that someones about

00:41:59.149 --> 00:42:01.418
to attack you, but
not completely sure of

00:42:01.452 --> 00:42:03.621
their intent,
it's a good idea to give

00:42:03.654 --> 00:42:06.156
them a warning before
pulling the trigger.

00:42:06.924 --> 00:42:11.295
Green laser pointers are a great
way to extend that courtesy.

00:42:11.829 --> 00:42:15.432
The marines like to call them
ocular interruption devices.

00:42:16.934 --> 00:42:19.870
Shine one in someone's
face and your target should

00:42:19.904 --> 00:42:23.307
immediately get the message
that it's time to back off.

00:42:24.041 --> 00:42:27.144
The LA9P made by B.
E. Meyers can warn

00:42:27.177 --> 00:42:30.814
people from up to 2
and a half miles away.

00:42:31.315 --> 00:42:34.885
It fires a 250 milliwatt beam.

00:42:34.919 --> 00:42:38.255
That's roughly one fourth the
strength smallest

00:42:38.289 --> 00:42:40.291
anti-aircraft lasers.

00:42:41.091 --> 00:42:43.494
Even so, you've got
to be careful when

00:42:43.527 --> 00:42:45.829
handling the thing.
Over a few months

00:42:45.863 --> 00:42:48.065
in Iraq,
a dozen soldiers were

00:42:48.098 --> 00:42:50.301
wounded in
dazzler friendly fire.

00:42:50.868 --> 00:42:52.937
Several troops may
have been injured

00:42:52.970 --> 00:42:55.372
while monkeying
around with laser target

00:42:55.406 --> 00:42:57.641
disintegrators which
are substantially

00:42:57.675 --> 00:43:00.377
more powerful than
the less lethal devices.

00:43:02.246 --> 00:43:05.583
And behold the Laser Avenger.
A cannon that can be used

00:43:05.616 --> 00:43:09.954
to take down incoming
enemy aircraft. Boeing was able

00:43:09.987 --> 00:43:13.357
to shoot a drone down out of
the sky with a Hummer mounted

00:43:13.390 --> 00:43:16.927
laser even though it's not
particularly high powered.

00:43:16.961 --> 00:43:19.863
It cooked the
remote control aircraft

00:43:19.897 --> 00:43:23.400
using a somewhat
feeble one-kilowatt beam.

00:43:25.235 --> 00:43:28.906
More recently, the company
shot down another UAV using

00:43:28.939 --> 00:43:32.576
a low-powered laser
paired with its mobile active

00:43:32.610 --> 00:43:35.946
targeting resource for
integrated experiments or

00:43:35.980 --> 00:43:39.984
matrix system during a test
in White Sands, New Mexico.

00:43:42.419 --> 00:43:44.722
Northrop Grumman
is hard at work on

00:43:44.755 --> 00:43:47.057
a 100 kilowatt
laser weapon which

00:43:47.091 --> 00:43:49.360
could do far more
damage but it's

00:43:49.393 --> 00:43:51.629
not quiet ready for prime time.

00:43:52.229 --> 00:43:55.499
It's fully operational but looks
like a refrigerator.

00:43:56.667 --> 00:43:59.403
Boeing announced
in December that the

00:43:59.436 --> 00:44:02.973
Avenger has been used
to destroy 50 different

00:44:03.007 --> 00:44:05.843
improvised explosive devices
during tests at

00:44:05.876 --> 00:44:09.113
Redstone Arsenal in Huntsville,
Alabama.

00:44:10.114 --> 00:44:11.215
[upbeat music]

00:44:28.032 --> 00:44:29.700
[disconcerting music]

00:44:40.377 --> 00:44:44.515
Science fiction has always been
a median for futuristic

00:44:44.548 --> 00:44:48.052
imagination. And while
different colored aliens and

00:44:48.085 --> 00:44:50.487
intergalactic
travel are yet to be

00:44:50.521 --> 00:44:54.625
discovered, there is an array of
technologies that are no longer

00:44:54.658 --> 00:44:57.227
figments of the
imagination thanks

00:44:57.261 --> 00:44:59.830
to the world of science fiction.

00:44:59.863 --> 00:45:02.166
Some of the creative inventions

00:45:02.199 --> 00:45:04.201
that have appeared
in family favorite

00:45:04.234 --> 00:45:06.336
movies like Back
to the Future and

00:45:06.370 --> 00:45:09.406
Total Recall are
now at the forefront

00:45:09.440 --> 00:45:11.608
of modern technology.

00:45:12.509 --> 00:45:15.779
While exploring space,
characters such as Captain

00:45:15.813 --> 00:45:20.784
Kirk and Spock would come across
alien life who spoke a different

00:45:20.818 --> 00:45:23.420
language.
To understand the galactic

00:45:23.454 --> 00:45:26.056
foreigners the Star
Trek characters

00:45:26.090 --> 00:45:28.358
used a device that immediately

00:45:28.392 --> 00:45:32.062
translated the aliens'
unusual language.

00:45:32.096 --> 00:45:35.132
Star Trek's Universal
Communicator

00:45:35.165 --> 00:45:37.234
was first seen on
screen as Spock

00:45:37.267 --> 00:45:40.037
tampered with it in
order to communicate

00:45:40.070 --> 00:45:43.040
with a non-biological entity.

00:45:43.073 --> 00:45:45.676
Although the idea
in Star Trek was to

00:45:45.709 --> 00:45:49.246
communicate with
intelligent alien life, a device

00:45:49.279 --> 00:45:52.316
capable of breaking
down language barriers

00:45:52.349 --> 00:45:55.419
would revolutionize
real time communication.

00:45:56.019 --> 00:45:59.590
Now products such
as SourceNex Pocket

00:45:59.623 --> 00:46:02.326
Talk and Skype's
new voice translation

00:46:02.359 --> 00:46:04.995
services are
capable of providing

00:46:05.028 --> 00:46:08.699
instantaneous translation
between languages.

00:46:09.600 --> 00:46:14.638
Flawless real-time communication
is far off but the technological

00:46:14.671 --> 00:46:17.207
advancements
over the last decade

00:46:17.241 --> 00:46:19.743
mean this feat is within reach.

00:46:21.411 --> 00:46:25.315
The idea behind
beaming someone up was

00:46:25.349 --> 00:46:27.618
that a person could
be broken down into

00:46:27.651 --> 00:46:30.587
an energy form and
then converted

00:46:30.621 --> 00:46:33.423
back into matter
at their destination.

00:46:33.457 --> 00:46:36.260
Transporting people
this way on Star

00:46:36.293 --> 00:46:39.029
Trek's USS Enterprise
had been around

00:46:39.062 --> 00:46:41.465
since the very beginning of the

00:46:41.498 --> 00:46:44.434
series,
debuting in the pilot episode.

00:46:46.770 --> 00:46:50.374
Scientists haven't figured
out how to transport humans

00:46:50.407 --> 00:46:53.977
yet but they can teleport
balls of energy known

00:46:54.011 --> 00:46:57.614
as photons. In this case
teleportation is based

00:46:57.648 --> 00:47:01.351
on a phenomenon know
as quantum entanglement.

00:47:01.919 --> 00:47:05.122
This refers to a condition
in quantum mechanics where

00:47:05.155 --> 00:47:08.826
two entangled
particles may be very far from

00:47:08.859 --> 00:47:11.995
one another yet remain
connected so that actions

00:47:12.029 --> 00:47:15.799
performed on one effect the
other regardless of distance.

00:47:16.400 --> 00:47:20.170
The information exchange
between the two photons occurs

00:47:20.204 --> 00:47:23.974
at least 10,000 times
faster than the speed of light.

00:47:26.577 --> 00:47:31.014
Not long into the first Star
Wars movie, Obi-Wan Kenobi

00:47:31.048 --> 00:47:35.986
receives a holographic message.
By definition, a hologram is

00:47:36.019 --> 00:47:38.622
a 3D image created from the

00:47:38.655 --> 00:47:40.891
interference of
light beams from a

00:47:40.924 --> 00:47:45.696
laser onto a 2D surfaces and
can only be seen in one angle.

00:47:47.898 --> 00:47:52.002
In 2018, researchers from
Brigham Young University

00:47:52.035 --> 00:47:56.173
in Utah created a real hologram.
Their technique

00:47:56.206 --> 00:48:01.078
called volumetric display
works like an Etch-a-Sketch

00:48:01.111 --> 00:48:04.114
toy but uses
particles at high speeds.

00:48:04.615 --> 00:48:08.785
With lasers, researchers can
trap particles and move them

00:48:08.819 --> 00:48:13.490
into a designated shape while
another set of lasers emit red,

00:48:13.523 --> 00:48:18.028
green and blue light into the
particle and create an image.

00:48:18.061 --> 00:48:22.499
But so far this can only happen
on extremely small scales.

00:48:24.801 --> 00:48:27.237
After losing his
hand Luke Skywalker

00:48:27.271 --> 00:48:30.274
receives a bionic
version that has all the

00:48:30.307 --> 00:48:33.310
functions of a normal hand.
This scenario

00:48:33.343 --> 00:48:36.380
is now more feasible
than the previous one.

00:48:37.147 --> 00:48:39.683
Researchers from the
Georgia University of

00:48:39.716 --> 00:48:43.120
Technology in Atlanta,
Georgia have been developing a

00:48:43.153 --> 00:48:46.356
way for amputees
to control each of their

00:48:46.390 --> 00:48:49.526
prosthetic fingers using
an ultra sonic sensor.

00:48:50.360 --> 00:48:54.398
In the movie Skywalker's
prosthesis uses electromagnetic

00:48:54.431 --> 00:48:57.434
sensors attached to his muscles.
The sensors

00:48:57.467 --> 00:49:00.871
can be switched into different
modes and are controlled

00:49:00.904 --> 00:49:04.074
by the flexing or
contracting of his muscles.

00:49:04.107 --> 00:49:06.710
The prosthesis
created by the Georgia

00:49:06.743 --> 00:49:09.313
Tech researchers,
however, uses machine

00:49:09.346 --> 00:49:11.748
learning and ultra
sound signals to

00:49:11.782 --> 00:49:14.551
detect fine finger
by finger movement.

00:49:17.087 --> 00:49:20.657
Orbiting Earth in 2001 a
Space Odyssey is Space

00:49:20.691 --> 00:49:24.194
Station V,
a large establishment located in

00:49:24.227 --> 00:49:27.564
low Earth orbit where
astronauts can bounce

00:49:27.597 --> 00:49:31.668
around in micro gravity.
Does this sound familiar?

00:49:31.902 --> 00:49:35.138
The Space Station V
provided inspiration for

00:49:35.172 --> 00:49:38.308
the International
Space Station which has

00:49:38.342 --> 00:49:41.945
been orbiting the Earth
since 1998 and currently

00:49:41.979 --> 00:49:45.182
accommodates up to
6 astronauts at a time.

00:49:45.849 --> 00:49:50.053
Although Space Station V
appears much more luxurious

00:49:50.087 --> 00:49:53.757
the ISS has accomplished
much more science.

00:49:53.790 --> 00:49:57.327
The ISS has been
fundamental in microgravity

00:49:57.361 --> 00:50:01.765
research since the start
of its construction in 1998.

00:50:04.034 --> 00:50:07.537
Tablets are wonderful hand
held computers that can

00:50:07.571 --> 00:50:11.074
be controlled at the press
of a finger. These handy

00:50:11.108 --> 00:50:14.811
devices are used by people
across the globe and even

00:50:14.845 --> 00:50:18.548
further upwards in the
International Space Station.

00:50:19.149 --> 00:50:22.152
Apple claims to
have invented the

00:50:22.185 --> 00:50:23.920
tablet with the
release of its iPad.

00:50:23.954 --> 00:50:27.157
However, Samsung
made an extremely

00:50:27.190 --> 00:50:29.860
interesting case
in court that Apple

00:50:29.893 --> 00:50:33.497
was wrong.
Stanley Kubrick and Sir

00:50:33.530 --> 00:50:37.401
Arthur C. Clarke did it by
including the device in the

00:50:37.434 --> 00:50:40.604
in the movie "2001:
A Space Odyssey"

00:50:40.637 --> 00:50:43.540
released in 1968. In the film,

00:50:43.573 --> 00:50:48.145
Dr. David Bowman and Dr. Frank
Poole watch news updates from

00:50:48.178 --> 00:50:52.983
their flat screen computers
which they called news pads.

00:50:53.417 --> 00:50:58.789
Samsung claimed that these news
pads were the original tablet

00:50:58.822 --> 00:51:01.792
featured in a film
over 40 years before

00:51:01.825 --> 00:51:04.895
the first iPad arrived in 2010.

00:51:05.829 --> 00:51:07.030
[curious music]

00:51:10.133 --> 00:51:13.503
We may even be
closer to an actual warp

00:51:13.537 --> 00:51:16.907
drive for space travel.
An ion thruster

00:51:16.940 --> 00:51:19.810
or ion drive is
a form of electric

00:51:19.843 --> 00:51:23.713
propulsion used for
space craft propulsion.

00:51:24.281 --> 00:51:26.583
It creates thrust
by accelerating

00:51:26.616 --> 00:51:28.385
ions using electricity.

00:51:28.952 --> 00:51:31.521
This engine was
used on Deep Space

00:51:31.555 --> 00:51:34.558
One and the Dawn
NASA spacecraft.

00:51:37.027 --> 00:51:41.431
A plasma propulsion engine
is a type of electric propulsion

00:51:41.465 --> 00:51:45.368
that generates thrust from
a quasi-neutral plasma.

00:51:46.536 --> 00:51:48.371
While most plasma engines are

00:51:48.405 --> 00:51:50.507
still confined to
the laboratory,

00:51:50.807 --> 00:51:54.578
some have been actively flying
and used on missions.

00:51:55.045 --> 00:51:58.782
As of 2011, NASA
partnered with the aerospace

00:51:58.815 --> 00:52:02.986
company Busek and
launched the first Hall Effect

00:52:03.019 --> 00:52:06.523
thruster, aboard the
TacSat-2 satellite. The

00:52:06.556 --> 00:52:11.061
thruster was the satellite's
main propulsion system.

00:52:11.895 --> 00:52:15.832
Actual warp drive is
still far into the future,

00:52:15.866 --> 00:52:18.535
but as more of these
advanced propulsion

00:52:18.568 --> 00:52:22.205
systems are developed,
the idea is not only

00:52:22.239 --> 00:52:26.610
feasible but now we know
it can actually be done.

00:52:27.244 --> 00:52:28.612
[dramatic sounds]

00:52:30.147 --> 00:52:33.817
Shrouded in mystery,
the existence of a secret

00:52:33.850 --> 00:52:37.420
space program is a
closely guarded secret.

00:52:37.621 --> 00:52:41.625
But information from government
whistle blowers, intelligence

00:52:41.658 --> 00:52:43.927
operatives,
and former astronauts

00:52:43.960 --> 00:52:46.163
have been surfacing for decades.

00:52:46.730 --> 00:52:49.599
In 2020,
America launched the Space

00:52:49.633 --> 00:52:53.036
Force,
a new branch of the US Military.

00:52:53.537 --> 00:52:56.773
Along with the Air Force
the new Space Force will

00:52:56.806 --> 00:53:00.076
be in charge of all military
needs in outer space.

00:53:00.777 --> 00:53:03.513
Many question the need for such
a program.

00:53:04.047 --> 00:53:06.416
We already had the Space Command

00:53:06.449 --> 00:53:09.653
department of the Air Force.
Some speculate

00:53:09.686 --> 00:53:12.923
the need may be a
fear of extra terrestrial

00:53:12.956 --> 00:53:15.825
invasion or influence
on the planet.

00:53:16.893 --> 00:53:17.961
[eery sounds]

00:53:19.896 --> 00:53:24.201
Technology already exists
for the new space force to take

00:53:24.234 --> 00:53:30.373
over. For example, the X37B
Space Plane is now in use.

00:53:31.541 --> 00:53:35.011
Much like the old
space shuttles, the X37B

00:53:35.045 --> 00:53:38.515
can be tasked with
several secret missions.

00:53:39.015 --> 00:53:41.685
Though it is unmanned, or so we
are told.

00:53:42.619 --> 00:53:44.921
The strange thing
about this space

00:53:44.955 --> 00:53:47.891
plane, is that its
mission is top secret.

00:53:48.191 --> 00:53:52.529
No one apart from a tiny
handful of top military

00:53:52.562 --> 00:53:56.800
experts know what the
aircraft is tasked to do.

00:53:57.400 --> 00:54:00.070
What we do know
is that the aircraft,

00:54:00.103 --> 00:54:02.739
also known as an
orbital test vehicle,

00:54:02.772 --> 00:54:05.475
will deploy a
satellite into orbit and

00:54:05.508 --> 00:54:08.144
also test power
beaming technology.

00:54:10.447 --> 00:54:12.816
The small plane is unmanned,
which

00:54:12.849 --> 00:54:15.018
means there are no astronauts

00:54:15.051 --> 00:54:19.456
on board the vehicle. It is
controlled remotely from Earth.

00:54:19.856 --> 00:54:22.058
It is able to fly back down to

00:54:22.092 --> 00:54:24.327
Earth and land
on a runway like a

00:54:24.361 --> 00:54:26.563
standard airplane. Meaning it

00:54:26.596 --> 00:54:28.798
can be re-launched
over and over.

00:54:34.104 --> 00:54:36.940
The pentagon,
a top military building where

00:54:36.973 --> 00:54:39.743
America's most
senior military officials

00:54:39.776 --> 00:54:42.112
work,
has revealed very few details

00:54:42.145 --> 00:54:45.248
about the aircraft's
missions in the past.

00:54:45.815 --> 00:54:48.351
Although it is
often referred to as

00:54:48.385 --> 00:54:50.920
a spy plane,
the US Air Force has

00:54:50.954 --> 00:54:53.423
never confirmed if the rocket is

00:54:53.456 --> 00:54:56.593
monitoring other
countries or satellites.

00:54:57.193 --> 00:55:00.130
Some experts have
previously said it would

00:55:00.163 --> 00:55:02.766
be difficult to monitor
other satellites. It

00:55:02.799 --> 00:55:06.102
should be noted also
that China has a secret

00:55:06.136 --> 00:55:09.105
space vehicle but
little is known about it.

00:55:11.374 --> 00:55:16.346
We may never know what the
secret mission really is.

00:55:16.379 --> 00:55:19.983
But the secret space program
goes much deeper than

00:55:20.016 --> 00:55:22.152
just one spy plane.

00:55:22.185 --> 00:55:25.555
Rumors have persisted
for decades that the

00:55:25.588 --> 00:55:28.958
USA has such a program.
Allegedly it began

00:55:28.992 --> 00:55:32.395
after the Roswell incident,
when America

00:55:32.429 --> 00:55:35.765
came into possession
of alien technology.

00:55:37.233 --> 00:55:39.302
There are those who claim
we have

00:55:39.336 --> 00:55:41.071
already been to the moon

00:55:41.104 --> 00:55:44.007
in the 1950's and
the NASA program

00:55:44.040 --> 00:55:46.276
was only for public consumption.

00:55:47.177 --> 00:55:49.879
Whistle blowers
have said we have

00:55:49.913 --> 00:55:52.615
time travel technology,
we've been

00:55:52.649 --> 00:55:56.820
to Mars and there is even a base
on the moon and Mars.

00:55:57.654 --> 00:56:00.757
Further down the rabbit hole,
is rumors that we

00:56:00.790 --> 00:56:03.526
actually fought
a war with aliens,

00:56:03.560 --> 00:56:06.296
and the secret space program is

00:56:06.329 --> 00:56:09.032
in place to protect
us from them.

00:56:11.134 --> 00:56:12.736
With Russian inspector

00:56:12.769 --> 00:56:15.171
satellites largely
believed to be

00:56:15.205 --> 00:56:19.242
orbital weapons platforms
and China now beginning to field

00:56:19.275 --> 00:56:23.079
its own maneuverable unmanned
orbital platforms that can

00:56:23.113 --> 00:56:27.350
also be used to disrupt our
nation's satellite capabilities,

00:56:27.584 --> 00:56:30.553
it's clear today
the United States is

00:56:30.587 --> 00:56:34.257
finding ways to fight
future wars in space.

00:56:34.724 --> 00:56:38.161
At least as far as
non-classified programs go.

00:56:38.695 --> 00:56:39.996
[dramatic music]

00:56:50.940 --> 00:56:54.477
Despite harsh statements made
by both Russian and Chinese

00:56:54.511 --> 00:56:58.648
government officials
regarding America's space force.

00:56:58.681 --> 00:57:01.951
Each of those nations
has already maintained

00:57:01.985 --> 00:57:05.321
space based branches
of their own for years.

00:57:06.055 --> 00:57:09.025
In fact, even
America once had a secretive

00:57:09.058 --> 00:57:12.095
Department of
Defense space program

00:57:12.562 --> 00:57:15.598
complete with its own military
astronauts.

00:57:15.865 --> 00:57:20.270
A 3.3 billion California based
space port

00:57:20.570 --> 00:57:23.173
meant for secretive
space shuttle

00:57:23.206 --> 00:57:25.875
launches into polar
orbit and more.

00:57:27.877 --> 00:57:31.514
The Endeavor was called the
manned space flight engineer

00:57:31.548 --> 00:57:35.251
program, and although it
hasn't gotten much attention

00:57:35.285 --> 00:57:38.755
in the years since,
the pentagon invested billions

00:57:38.788 --> 00:57:42.258
of dollars into it throughout
the 1970's and 80's.

00:57:42.992 --> 00:57:45.695
A secret group of
32 men was selected

00:57:45.728 --> 00:57:48.164
from the U.S. Air Force

00:57:48.198 --> 00:57:50.733
and trained as
astronauts completely

00:57:50.767 --> 00:57:53.670
independent of
their peers at NASA.

00:57:54.437 --> 00:57:56.973
The specialized
training revolved

00:57:57.006 --> 00:58:00.043
around deploying
classified payloads

00:58:00.076 --> 00:58:02.545
and conducting other secretive

00:58:02.579 --> 00:58:05.482
activities in orbit
using America's

00:58:05.515 --> 00:58:08.351
space shuttle as
the primary orbital

00:58:08.384 --> 00:58:10.887
platform. In fact, at one time,

00:58:10.920 --> 00:58:13.256
the DOD intended to fly more

00:58:13.289 --> 00:58:16.226
shuttle flights per
year than NASA.

00:58:18.228 --> 00:58:19.562
[laid back music]

00:58:19.762 --> 00:58:23.132
Black Star is the reported
codename of a secret

00:58:23.166 --> 00:58:26.436
United States orbital
space plane system.

00:58:27.036 --> 00:58:31.574
The possible existence of the
Black Star program was reported

00:58:31.608 --> 00:58:36.212
in March of 2006 by Aviation
Week and Space Technology
magazine.

00:58:36.946 --> 00:58:41.050
The magazine reported that the
program had been under way since

00:58:41.084 --> 00:58:43.987
at least the early
1990's and that

00:58:44.020 --> 00:58:46.256
the impetus for Black Star was

00:58:46.289 --> 00:58:48.858
to allow the United
States government

00:58:48.892 --> 00:58:51.227
to retain orbital reconnaissance

00:58:51.261 --> 00:58:53.763
capabilities
jeopardized following

00:58:53.796 --> 00:58:56.065
the 1986 Challenger disaster.

00:58:56.799 --> 00:58:59.602
The article also said
the United States Air

00:58:59.636 --> 00:59:02.805
Force Space Command
was unaware of Black Star.

00:59:03.206 --> 00:59:06.709
Suggesting it was
operated by an intelligence

00:59:06.743 --> 00:59:10.179
agency or some other
secret space program.

00:59:11.748 --> 00:59:14.617
Aviation Week
speculated that such a

00:59:14.651 --> 00:59:17.520
space craft could
also have offensive

00:59:17.554 --> 00:59:20.023
military capabilities. A concept

00:59:20.056 --> 00:59:23.459
colloquially known
as the space bomber.

00:59:23.960 --> 00:59:26.829
The magazine also
stated that it was likely

00:59:26.863 --> 00:59:29.365
that Black Star
would be moth balled,

00:59:29.399 --> 00:59:32.068
although it is
unclear whether this is

00:59:32.101 --> 00:59:34.804
due to a cost or
failure of the program.

00:59:35.505 --> 00:59:36.773
[dramatic music]

00:59:38.141 --> 00:59:40.777
A secret space
program was revealed

00:59:40.810 --> 00:59:43.446
to the worldwide
public following

00:59:43.479 --> 00:59:46.316
allegations against
Gary McKinnon for

00:59:46.349 --> 00:59:49.652
hacking the US Defense
programs in 2002.

00:59:50.753 --> 00:59:55.558
In an interview televised
on the BBC, McKinnon

00:59:55.592 --> 00:59:58.394
stated that he was
able to get into the

00:59:58.428 --> 01:00:02.265
military's network simply
by using a computer

01:00:02.298 --> 01:00:06.002
code familiar to
computer administrators.

01:00:06.703 --> 01:00:09.839
In his interview
with the BBC he also

01:00:09.872 --> 01:00:13.176
stated of the disclosure
project that "They

01:00:13.209 --> 01:00:16.279
are some very credible
relied upon people

01:00:16.312 --> 01:00:20.583
all saying yes. There
is UFO technology.

01:00:21.050 --> 01:00:23.586
There's anti-gravity,
there's free

01:00:23.620 --> 01:00:26.122
energy and it's
extra terrestrial

01:00:26.155 --> 01:00:28.725
in origin and they've
captured space

01:00:28.758 --> 01:00:31.260
craft and reverse
engineered it."

01:00:32.395 --> 01:00:36.633
He said he investigated a
NASA photographic expert's claim

01:00:36.666 --> 01:00:40.903
that at the Johnson Space
Center's building 8, images were

01:00:40.937 --> 01:00:45.408
regularly cleaned of evidence
of UFO craft and he confirmed

01:00:45.441 --> 01:00:49.912
this comparing the raw originals
with the processed images.

01:00:51.047 --> 01:00:54.017
He stated to have
viewed a detailed image of

01:00:54.050 --> 01:00:57.553
something not man made
and cigar shaped, floating

01:00:57.587 --> 01:01:01.024
above the northern hemisphere
and assuming his viewing

01:01:01.057 --> 01:01:04.427
would be undisrupted
owing to the hour, he did

01:01:04.460 --> 01:01:07.897
not think of capturing
the image because he was

01:01:07.930 --> 01:01:11.334
bedazzled and therefore
did not think of securing

01:01:11.367 --> 01:01:14.904
it with a screen capture
function in the software

01:01:14.937 --> 01:01:18.207
at the point his
connection was interrupted.

01:01:19.409 --> 01:01:22.645
McKinnon described the
cigar shaped space craft in

01:01:22.679 --> 01:01:25.882
rudimentary terms but
with some notable features

01:01:25.915 --> 01:01:28.985
that paralleled other
witnesses description of

01:01:29.018 --> 01:01:32.055
an existing cylindrical
space craft.

01:01:32.488 --> 01:01:33.523
[tense music]

01:01:34.524 --> 01:01:38.061
One of the most
interesting things about this

01:01:38.094 --> 01:01:41.364
was a Microsoft Excel
spreadsheet he came

01:01:41.397 --> 01:01:45.101
across with 20-30 names
of government officials

01:01:45.134 --> 01:01:48.671
that was titled
"Non-terrestrial officers".

01:01:50.106 --> 01:01:54.077
What's more intriguing,
according to reports McKinnon

01:01:54.110 --> 01:01:58.081
also discovered an unusual
list of US Navy vessels.

01:01:58.581 --> 01:02:00.550
But cross checking against the

01:02:00.583 --> 01:02:02.885
active list of
surface ships and

01:02:02.919 --> 01:02:05.555
submarines, McKinnon
could not find those

01:02:05.588 --> 01:02:08.057
names on the current
US Navy roster.

01:02:08.791 --> 01:02:13.029
What does this mean?
The list of non-terrestrial

01:02:13.062 --> 01:02:16.933
officers is alleged by
many UFO researchers

01:02:16.966 --> 01:02:20.703
to be the names of US
Navy and Air Force

01:02:20.737 --> 01:02:25.074
officers who are serving
on ships off the Earth.

01:02:25.842 --> 01:02:30.480
That's to say they are assigned
to interplanetary vessels.

01:02:31.180 --> 01:02:35.918
Additionally, the names of
the ships that he found are

01:02:35.952 --> 01:02:38.755
actually the names
of interplanetary

01:02:38.788 --> 01:02:41.424
spaceships currently in service.

01:02:41.758 --> 01:02:42.792
[tense music]

01:02:44.026 --> 01:02:47.997
Is it possible we have an active
interplanetary space force

01:02:48.030 --> 01:02:52.068
already being utilized for
the protection of the Earth?

01:02:52.935 --> 01:02:55.571
We certainly have
the technology to build and

01:02:55.605 --> 01:02:58.241
maintain such a force.
The key would

01:02:58.274 --> 01:03:00.777
be in the billions
allocated to the

01:03:00.810 --> 01:03:03.346
dark military budget in the USA.

01:03:04.380 --> 01:03:07.383
With enough money,
you could build several

01:03:07.416 --> 01:03:10.386
fleets and the black
budget has plenty.

01:03:10.987 --> 01:03:12.188
[ominous music]

01:03:13.289 --> 01:03:16.826
Technology has the
power to do many things

01:03:16.859 --> 01:03:20.296
and changing the
world is one of them.

01:03:20.763 --> 01:03:23.232
We're privileged to live in a
time where

01:03:23.266 --> 01:03:26.202
science and
technology can assist us,

01:03:26.235 --> 01:03:28.738
make our lives
easier and rethink

01:03:28.771 --> 01:03:31.641
the ways we go
about our daily lives.

01:03:32.208 --> 01:03:35.878
The technology we're already
exposed and accustomed

01:03:35.912 --> 01:03:39.549
to has paved the way for
us to innovate further and

01:03:39.582 --> 01:03:43.419
this list of current and
future technologies certainly

01:03:43.452 --> 01:03:46.989
have the potential to
change our lives even more.

01:03:47.924 --> 01:03:50.626
We may even be
closer to that flying

01:03:50.660 --> 01:03:53.062
car you were
promised as a child.

01:03:53.830 --> 01:03:55.431
They do exist today.

01:03:56.999 --> 01:03:59.468
However,
with all innovations it

01:03:59.502 --> 01:04:02.238
will depend on what
we do with them.

01:04:02.772 --> 01:04:05.708
They can either enhance
our lives and make the

01:04:05.741 --> 01:04:09.712
world a better place to live
or we may find ourselves

01:04:09.745 --> 01:04:12.982
in a dystopian future
where we are ruled and

01:04:13.015 --> 01:04:16.986
controlled by the very
technologies we rely on.

01:04:17.587 --> 01:04:21.657
That is up to us and
how we manage an ever

01:04:21.691 --> 01:04:25.828
changing world with
advanced technology.

01:04:26.529 --> 01:04:27.730
[ominous music]

